---
/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bed availability.

   The largest remaining topic in the export: 108 of 571 Buena Vista calls
   (18.9%) ask about beds, and 53 (9.3%) are told there is nothing that day.
   P0 in the sitemap.

   ⚠ PUBLISHES NO NUMBERS, DELIBERATELY. The wiki census (detox 15/35, RTC
   15/39) is from July and would be stale and misleading. A count that is wrong
   by an afternoon is worse than none, because someone decides whether to call
   based on it. The page's whole argument is that the phone is the only current
   source — do not "improve" it by adding a live-looking figure unless it is
   genuinely wired to the census.

   DIFFERENTIATION from the summary section on /admissions/: this page explains
   WHY the answer moves. The four moving parts — detox turning over faster than
   residential, separate men's and women's wings, level-of-care match, and
   coverage — are the non-obvious content. The gender-wing point in particular
   explains why two callers an hour apart get different answers.

   Being told full is treated as a common outcome rather than an edge case,
   because roughly one in ten callers hears it. The withdrawal safety note at
   the end of WhenWereFull matters: someone told no should not simply wait it
   out at home.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TopBar from '../../components/TopBar.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';

import BedsHero from '../../components/beds/BedsHero.astro';
import WhyItMoves from '../../components/beds/WhyItMoves.astro';
import WhenWereFull from '../../components/beds/WhenWereFull.astro';
import BedsQuestions from '../../components/beds/BedsQuestions.astro';

import Testimonials from '../../components/Testimonials.astro';
import VerifySection from '../../components/VerifySection.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../../components/FinalCTA.astro';

const title = 'Bed Availability | Buena Vista Health & Recovery, Chandler AZ';
const description =
  'Detox and residential bed availability at our Chandler, AZ facility changes daily. Call (888) 362-5576 for today’s answer, your level of care and a coverage check in one call.';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    ['Does Buena Vista have beds available?',
     'Availability changes daily and separately for detox and residential care, so the current answer comes from admissions on the phone. A call gives you today’s position along with a coverage check.'],
    ['How quickly can I be admitted if a bed is open?',
     'Often the same day. When a bed is open and coverage is confirmed, admission can happen that day, with travel arranged as part of the same call.'],
    ['Why do two people get different answers about beds?',
     'Housing is not co-ed, so a bed opening on the men’s wing does not help a woman waiting. Detox and residential availability also move independently, as detox stays are days and residential stays are weeks.'],
    ['What happens if you are full?',
     'Your file is opened anyway so the assessment and coverage check hold, admissions calls you back when a bed frees up, and in the meantime help you find a programme with space now if waiting is not realistic.'],
  ].map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <TopBar />
  <Nav />

  <BedsHero />
  <WhyItMoves />
  <WhenWereFull />
  <Testimonials />
  <VerifySection />
  <BedsQuestions />

  <FinalCTA />

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} is:inline />
</Layout>
